                <pb facs="0425" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7353b W 52/186: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-18T18:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 18,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 18—5:03
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>561. Foreign Office informs me that it has advised British Minister to Portugal
                    regarding signing on December 10 of agreement by the Western Union, Italian, and
                    the Western Telegraph Companies and has instructed him not to oppose any longer
                    the Western Union concession.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Legation in Portugal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
